X-SOURCE-ID:montclairlocal
X-SOURCE:Montclair Local News
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260528T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260528T210000
DTSTAMP:20260527T003021
CREATED:20260523T022013Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260523T022013Z
UID:10140001-1779991200-1780002000@montclairlocal.news
SUMMARY:You Hear Songs\, I See Them: Art\, Music\, and Synesthesia – An Experience with Sarah Kraning
DESCRIPTION:Step into an evening where music becomes color\, movement\, and art. Artist Sarah Kraning experiences sound through synesthesia\, perceiving music as vivid colors\, textures\, and motion that she transforms into large-scale paintings. In conversation with Montclair Art Museum (MAM) Executive Director Todd Caissie\, Kraning will discuss her experience with synesthesia and how it has shaped her artistic practice\, exploring the connections between art\, perception\, creativity\, and mental health awareness. The evening culminates in a live painting performance as Kraning transforms a Taylor Swift song into an original artwork in real time before the audience. The finished piece will be available through an online auction open to attendees through the weekend. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/you-hear-songs-i-see-them-art-music-and-synesthesia-an-experience-with-sarah-kraning/
LOCATION:Montclair Art Museum\, 3 South Mountain Ave\, Montclair\, NJ\, 07042\, United States
CATEGORIES:Art & Culture,Entertainment
GEO:40.8185787;-74.2242523
