DTSTAMP:20260601T000000Z
SUMMARY:1776 in Western America: Forts\, Furs and Frontier Online NEW
DESCRIPTION:This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\nIn 1776\, while the 13 colonies were rising up against 
 Britain\, the rest of North America was occupied by a mixture of empires 
 competing through an interconnected web of conquest\, exploration\, 
 settlement and trade. From the Spanish missions in California to Native 
 American trade centers on the Missouri River\, Captain Cook’s voyage up 
 the Pacific Coast in search of the Northwest Passage\, Russian forays to 
 Alaska for sea otter pelts\, the Hudson Bay Company’s quest for fur-trade 
 dominance\, and the expanding Plains empire of the Comanche\, we will 
 explore how diverse peoples shaped a continent in flux. Maps\, images and 
 discussion will illuminate the year 1776 as both a revolutionary and 
 continental turning point in the story of North America.
LOCATION:Montclair - Offsite\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Lectures / History & Culture
UID:LibCal-10306-16582481
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16582481
END:VEVENT
