SUMMARY:Spring Birding Class - Birds & Their Nests
DESCRIPTION:FREE Spring Birding Classes – Adults \nExplore the world of birds in the beautiful gardens of Van Vleck. Each class will focus on a specific topic to help us learn more about these amazing creatures. Weather permitting\, a birding walk will be included so bring your binoculars (or borrow a pair from Van Vleck) and join us for some birding fun. Instructor: Naturalist Jenny Aley\, Van Vleck Education Volunteer. \nNow June 2nd – 9:00 AM -10:00 AM – Birds and their Nests – Examine various bird nests and look at how birds prepare for their new families. \nOpen to adults. Space is limited – register early.   \nFree – Registration required – no drop-ins for this class. \n \nJune 27th – 9:00-10:00 AM – Young Birds – Sharpen your identification skills by focusing on young birds who don’t look exactly like adults yet.
URL:https://montclairfoundation.org/event/spring-birding-class-birds-their-nests/
LOCATION:Van Vleck House & Gardens\, 21 Van Vleck Street\, Montclair\, 07042\, United States
CATEGORIES:Classes,Adults
