SUMMARY:The Country vs. the City: Bridging the Rural-Urban Divide NEW
DESCRIPTION:This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\nAt a time when the split between rural areas and urban areas 
 in the United States threatens to upend our democracy\, what can city 
 people learn about country people that might help bridge the gap? What do 
 rural people want? Why are urban people prejudiced against them? How can we 
 learn who country people are and what they want\, given the fact that they 
 don't write their own history? Why do country people seem conservative\, 
 and city people seem progressive? \n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School
