SUMMARY:All Our Voices - Story Gardeners: World Storytellers Workshop (for Parents-Adults)
DESCRIPTION:Montclair Public Library offers children's storytimes in many 
 languages and cultures. Are you someone who wants to share your culture 
 through storytelling? Ana Cristina Coura and Sabina Wasonga-Gitau\, master 
 storytellers of Portuguese and Swahili storytimes\, lead a hands-on 
 workshop for adults interested in conducting children’s storytimes in 
 other languages and cultures. Engage in this interactive session designed 
 to bring forth your inner storyteller with confidence! Registration is 
 required.\n\nStoryteller Bios:\nAna Cristina Coura\, is an educator with a 
 background in psychology who has taught children in Brazil and worked as an 
 art educator.\n\n\n\nSabina Wasonga-Gitau is an educator and a storyteller. 
 She is a native Swahili speaker. Her interest in sharing her culture has 
 led her to infuse the Swahili language in her storytelling. She is a Folk 
 artist with The Folklife Center of Northern New Jersey. A recipient of the 
 New Jersey State Council on the Arts (Folk Arts Apprenticeship Grant). 
 Wasonga-Gitau  sits on the Board of The Diversity Center - (connecting 
 communities through culture)\n\nShe has told stories  online and in person 
 at Public Libraries\, Colleges\, Middle Schools and Elementary Schools. She 
 has performed at the UN during World Kiswahili Day and at the Montclair 
 Literary Festival. She believes everyone has a story.\n\n \n\n\n\n*The 
 Montclair Public Library's All Our Voices World Languages Collection for 
 Children is generously sponsored by Dumpling Diplomacy of Montclair.\n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Green Room\, Montclair Main - Storytime Room
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Children's Programs, Language, Personal Growth, Storytime, Talk, Story Time
UID:LibCal-10306-16682427
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16682427
END:VEVENT
