SUMMARY:Breaking the Burnout Cycle: Tools for Lasting Change NEW
DESCRIPTION:This is a free Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\nBurnout is a serious issue affecting many of us. It is 
 characterized by fatigue\, low productivity and feeling disconnected at 
 work. The effects of burnout extend beyond personal challenges\; they can 
 negatively impact overall health\, leading to higher absenteeism\, high 
 turnover rate\, workplace conflicts and low job satisfaction. Now more than 
 ever\, it’s essential to take proactive steps. Explore proven strategies 
 to combat burnout\, uplift team morale\, and foster a culture of openness. 
 When we create space for honest conversations and prioritize well-being\, 
 we build stronger\, more resilient teams.\n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Conference Room\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School
UID:LibCal-10306-16394867
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16394867
END:VEVENT
