UID:10007135-1780750800-1780758000@montclairfoundation.org
SUMMARY:Scout Program: Insect Exploration
DESCRIPTION:Scout Program – Insect Exploration  \n June 6th\, 1:00 PM – 3:00 PM  \n\nJoin us for our last scout day of the season on Saturday June 6th\, Insect Exploration. Open to scout troops and scouts attending with their families.\n\nHave you ever wondered what critters are crawling and flying around the gardens? Discover what insects can be found in the gardens. Learn about local insects and pollinators\, draw and journal about the bugs you find with your fellow scouts\, and take part in our wildflower meadow citizen science project.This program is open to all scouts of all levels\, and would fulfill the requirements for the Brownie Bugs badge and portions of the Scouting America Insect Study badge. \nFee: $10 per scout. Leaders/adult chaperones free of charge for this program\, (minimum 2 chaperones per troop) \nRegistration Information: \n-Registration by Troop Leaders only – No individual scout registrations \nTo request a spot for your troop: \n1 – Complete Information by clicking on the link below starting \n2 – Payment link will be emailed to you as space allows on a first come first serve basis. \n \n 
