SUMMARY:But I'm A Cheerleader (1999) - Laugh Out Loud Pride Film Screenings
DESCRIPTION:This is a free Adult School class. Click below to 
 register.\n\nJoin us for a screening the cult classic film\, "But I'm A 
 Cheerleader" to kick off Pride this year at Montclair Public Library! The 
 screening will be followed by a open panel discussion about the film with 
 queer film maker Abigail Espinal and FDU Professor Cordelia Siporin. Free 
 snacks and drinks will be provided by Lotus Lemonade & Kettecorn. These 
 screenings are proudly co-presented by Pride Center of Montclair. Come join 
 in the fun and bring a friend!\n\n"A naive teenager is sent to "sexual 
 redirection" camp when her straitlaced parents and friends suspect her of 
 being gay. With Natasha Lyonne."
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Books, Film & Theater
