SUMMARY:(FULL) Everything Book Club\, "Bel Canto" by Ann Patchett
DESCRIPTION:Don't miss the Library's Open Book / Open Mind program with Ann 
 Patchett about her newest book\, "Whistler" on Thursday\, June 2\, two days 
 after publication! Tickets cost $35 and include a pre-signed copy of the 
 book. Register at tinyurl.com/OBOMPatchett\n\nIn our discussion\, we'll 
 talk about Patchett's conversation as well as "Bel Canto\," her beloved 
 breakthrough bestseller about a group of international guests taken hostage 
 by terrorists at a birthday party concert in South America\, who 
 unexpectedly find deep bonds\, friendship\, and even love over several 
 months of captivity. If you've always meant to read it\, now's your chance. 
 If you've read it before\, let's enjoy it again together!\n\n"'Bel Canto' 
 is its own universe. A marvel of a book." —Washington Post Book 
 World\n\nAnn Patchett is the #1 bestselling author of seven novels. She 
 writes for the New York Times Magazine\, Elle\, GQ\, the Financial Times\, 
 the Paris Review and Vogue. She lives in Nashville\, Tennessee\, where she 
 co-owns Parnassus Bookstore.\n\n
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Tower Room\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult Services, Book Discussion
UID:LibCal-10306-15960780
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/15960780
END:VEVENT
